cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this toolkit, please cite it as below."
title: "keyspace-audit: measuring realized entropy and detecting keyspace collapse"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-23
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >-
  A dependency-light toolkit for measuring the realized (as opposed to nominal)
  keyspace of a seed generator, detecting keyspace collapse, and demonstrating
  that XOR whitening against a fixed keystream adds zero entropy. Includes a
  reference Yasmarang PRNG, a vectorised twin with a bit-exact self-test, a
  black-box realized-keyspace auditor, and a generic OpenCL keystream kernel with
  a GPU/CPU bit-exactness self-test. Deliberately excludes device seeding models,
  key derivation, and target matching.
keywords:
  - pseudo-random number generator
  - entropy estimation
  - keyspace collapse
  - hardware wallet security
  - reproducible security research
